# Keep the Vercel deployment frontend-only.
#
# Root cause of the 2026-09 static-asset 404 outage: Vercel's zero-config Python
# runtime auto-detects ANY requirements.txt/pyproject.toml/Pipfile plus a matching
# entrypoint file (app.py, main.py, etc. -- including the same names inside an
# `app/` or `src/` folder, e.g. this repo's app/main.py) and deploys the WHOLE
# repo as a Vercel Function that receives every request. That silently overrode
# vercel.json's `outputDirectory: "static"` static hosting, and the `/static/:path*`
# rewrite (correct for pure static hosting) then stripped the `/static` prefix
# before the request reached the running FastAPI app, which only serves assets
# under the `/static` mount -- producing FastAPI's own JSON 404 for every asset.
#
# The real backend is Render (see render.yaml / DEPLOYMENT.md); Vercel must only
# ever serve the static/ control room and call the Render API. Excluding the
# Python surface below prevents Vercel from ever re-detecting it as a backend to
# run, regardless of dashboard Framework Preset settings.
app/
kaizen_active/
kaizen_ai/
kaizen_arena/
kaizen_cape/
kaizen_control/
kaizen_data/
kaizen_factory/
kaizen_ie/
kaizen_investigator/
kaizen_optimizer/
kaizen_quality/
kaizen_simulation/
kaizen_version.py
requirements.txt
requirements-dev.txt
pytest.ini
render.yaml
tests/
scripts/
data/
docs/
artifacts/
campaign/
empirical/
examples/
intelligence/
tenx/
tenx_ui/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
.github/
start.sh
start_kaizen.ps1
START_KAIZEN.bat
.env.example
PROJECT_METADATA.json
RELEASE_MANIFEST.json
SOURCE_SHA256SUMS.json
VERSION
README.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
LICENSE
